# PS4 Mem API sample calls (VS Code REST Client, JetBrains HTTP client or Visual Studio).
# Start the API first:  dotnet run --project src/PS4Mem.Api
# Errors come back as {"error": "..."}: 400 bad input, 409 not connected / already connected,
# 502 the PS4 refused or didn't answer.
# The tests replay this file top to bottom against a fake console, so keep every call working.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:5080
# A pid from GET /api/processes (the game you chose).
@pid = 85

### Connection state, and the IP a connect would use
GET {{host}}/api/status

### Saved settings
GET {{host}}/api/settings

### Change some settings (only the fields you send change)
# Other fields: consoleIp, commandPort, loaderPort (9090 GoldHEN; 9020/9021 other loaders), payloadPath.
PUT {{host}}/api/settings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debugLogging": false
}

### Inject the payload, wait for ps4debug (up to 20 s), then connect. Once per PS4 session:
# BinLoader takes one payload, then refuses until it's toggled in GoldHEN or the PS4 restarts.
# 409 if ps4debug already answers: use Connect instead (a second copy can freeze the console).
# Optional: {"ip": "<PS4_IP>", "payloadPath": "/path/to/ps4debug.bin", "loaderPort": 9090};
# a path and port that work are saved.
POST {{host}}/api/inject
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Status again: connected, with the ps4debug version
GET {{host}}/api/status

### Every process; the likely game has "suggested": true and a reason (you still choose)
GET {{host}}/api/processes

### Process info: name, path and title ID
GET {{host}}/api/processes/{{pid}}

### Sections with the default selection and each section's reason
GET {{host}}/api/processes/{{pid}}/maps

### Your own name filter (empty = any name), and read-only sections too
GET {{host}}/api/processes/{{pid}}/maps?filter=anon,exe&includeReadOnly=true

### Select every section
GET {{host}}/api/processes/{{pid}}/maps?all=true

### Disconnect (always 200)
POST {{host}}/api/disconnect

### Connect when the payload is already running. With no ip this uses PS4_IP, then
# ps4ip.local, then the saved IP. To pick the IP yourself, send {"ip": "<PS4_IP>"} instead.
POST {{host}}/api/connect
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Disconnect again
POST {{host}}/api/disconnect
